WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:15.643
SHOW ONLY THE KINDS PACKAGE
⊞ on Kinds shows only it in the diagrams. Kinds declares the #Tag keywords the model uses: layer, role, mode and lifecycle tags.

2
00:00:15.643 --> 00:00:30.506
GENERAL VIEW
One metadata definition per tag: the five layers, then Mission, Actor, Mode, Hazard, MoE, Budget and more. The model imports Kinds at its root, so #MoE or #Hazard anywhere names one of these.

3
00:00:30.506 --> 00:00:40.885
TREE VIEW
Tree shows what Kinds contains: its 33 tags and nothing else. General and Tree are the only views that show anything for Kinds.

4
00:00:40.885 --> 00:00:52.535
SHOW ONLY COMMON
⊞ on Common. It holds what every layer shares: the items that flow, the ports and interfaces they cross, and the measures of effectiveness.

5
00:00:52.535 --> 00:01:04.659
TREE VIEW
Its 116 members hang off one package. Zoomed in: each measure of effectiveness, an «attribute», is followed by the «constraint» holding it to its target.

6
00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:17.383
GENERAL VIEW
Definitions as boxes, attributes listed inside. Selected, CoordinationMessage is the hub: eight message kinds specialise it, so one mesh port carries them all.

7
00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:28.784
PUT AN ATTRIBUTE BACK
Before recording we deleted sequenceNumber from CoordinationMessage, which now lists only senderId and sentAt. Now we add it back.

8
00:01:28.784 --> 00:01:39.768
PLACE AN ATTRIBUTE
Pick Attribute in the palette, then click the definition box: a new attribute is created inside it and selected, ready to name.

9
00:01:39.768 --> 00:01:52.480
NAME IT AND TYPE IT
In Properties: the name sequenceNumber, then the type ScalarValues::Integer, from the standard library; Enter binds it. The box lists it as name : type.

10
00:01:52.480 --> 00:02:05.044
DOCUMENT IT
The documentation goes in the same panel, word for word as before: where the message sits in the sender's stream.

11
00:02:05.044 --> 00:02:17.102
THE RESULT
CoordinationMessage lists senderId, sentAt and sequenceNumber again, and the diagram is as it was. Edits stay in this browser until you Save or Export.

12
00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:29.956
INTERCONNECTION VIEW
Interconnection is for parts and their connections, and Common has neither. It shows the 25 items declared inside its ports and definitions, unconnected.

13
00:02:29.956 --> 00:02:40.426
REQUIREMENT VIEW
Common's 22 require constraints: 12 hold a measure of effectiveness to its target, 10 hold a budget that the brief fixes.

14
00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:54.235
READ ONE CONSTRAINT
Select one and zoom in to read it: areaUnderWatchTarget, areaUnderWatchFraction ≥ 0.9, at least 0.9 of the area under watch at any moment. Each box shows its condition.

15
00:02:54.235 --> 00:03:07.835
PARAMETRIC VIEW
Parametric is where values are bound to constraints, with the Bind tool. Common binds none, so it shows the same 22 constraints, each with its condition, standing alone.
